Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch (no real network calls), covering: URL/header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error rejection, missing API key errors, malformed response handling, and mock-mode behavior verification.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach fetch restoration — no real network calls in any test
- Test verifies searchFlights constructs the correct RapidAPI URL and headers (including X-RapidAPI-Key) when making a real fetch call
- Test verifies a successful API response is correctly parsed into FlightResult[] matching the exported interface shape
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error whose message includes the status code and does not include the apiKey value
- Test verifies missing or empty-string apiKey (constructor arg and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var) causes SkyscannerClient constructor to throw a descriptive missing-key Error
- Test verifies malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' causes searchFlights to return deterministic fixture data without invoking fetch (fetch spy asserted not called); test verifies non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') result in a real fetch call
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 with no type errors; vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts { apiKey?: string } object parameter, defaults to empty object
- Constructor resolves apiKey from: 1) constructor option, 2) process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY, 3) empty string
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'SkyscannerClient requires an apiKey. Provide it via constructor option { apiKey } or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when resolvedApiKey is falsy or empty string
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- searchFlights checks process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (strict equality, case-sensitive) to return mock data
- Mock mode returns exactly 3 FlightResult objects from getMockFlightResults() with prices 299, 450, 189
- Non-'true' values for MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API (including 'TRUE', '1', 'false', empty string, undefined) result in real fetch call
- Real API URL: https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/search with query params origin, destination, date, adults
- Request headers include: 'X-RapidAPI-Key', 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com', 'Accept': 'application/json'
- HTTP error throws Error with message: 'Skyscanner API request failed with status ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}'
- Error messages do NOT include apiKey value - apiKey is only used in header, never in error messages
- Network errors throw Error with message: 'Network error while calling Skyscanner API: ${error.message}'
- parseFlightResults validates response is object, then extracts results from data.results || data.data || data
- parseFlightResults validates each result has: price, airline, departure, arrival, duration, stops - throws 'Invalid API response: missing X field' if absent
- parseFlightResults handles case-insensitive field names: price/Price, currency/Currency, airline/Airline/carrier/Carrier, departure/Departure/departureTime/DepartureTime, arrival/Arrival/arrivalTime/ArrivalTime, duration/Duration/flightDuration/FlightDuration, stops/Stops/numberOfStops/NumberOfStops
- extractNumber returns undefined for non-numeric values; extractString returns empty string for null/undefined
- currency defaults to 'USD' if missing; airline defaults to empty string if missing

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
